   </table><p style="text-indent:4.533%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="text-indent:2.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue increased for the three months ended June 30, 2026, from the three months ended June 30, 2025. The change related to an increase of $2.9 million in web hosting costs from increased activity in the current year and the expiration of usage credits in the prior period and an increase in allocated overhead costs of $0.3 million.</span></p><p style="text-indent:2.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue increased for the six months ended June 30, 2026, from the six months ended June 30, 2025. The change was due to an increase of $5.5 million in web hosting costs from increased activity in the current year and the expiration of usage credits utilized in the prior period, as well as increased allocated overhead costs of $1.0 million.</span></p><p style="text-indent:2.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">We expect cost of revenue to remain consistent in the near term in both absolute dollars and as a percentage of revenue.</span></p></div>
